      "id": "37130552",
      "title": "Instance Variables (Properties) & Configurable Widgets",
      "lectureOrder": 43,
      "videoOrder": 40,
      "sourceHash": "147c334b5ec435b24ec732a1d59964bcc935b6fc2d3773453f1b149b5569474a",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.04,
          "end": 4.65,
          "en": "So now that we learned about variables,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.65,
          "end": 7.14,
          "en": "let's use this variables feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.14,
          "end": 10.2,
          "en": "to make some of our code more reusable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.2,
          "end": 13.02,
          "en": "like for example, the styled text widget.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.02,
          "end": 15,
          "en": "We created a custom widget here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15,
          "end": 18.45,
          "en": "so that we have this reusable style text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.45,
          "end": 22.14,
          "en": "But at the moment, this is only partially reusable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.14,
          "end": 25.62,
          "en": "if we're honest, because 'Hello World!' is hard-coded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.62,
          "end": 27.87,
          "en": "in this code snippet here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.87,
          "end": 31.98,
          "en": "So whenever we use style text anywhere in our application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.98,
          "end": 35.28,
          "en": "it'll always output 'Hello World!'",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.28,
          "end": 37.26,
          "en": "Now the idea behind this custom wigit,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.26,
          "end": 39.57,
          "en": "it is probably that we want to be able",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.57,
          "end": 42.39,
          "en": "to reuse this configuration for this text,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.39,
          "end": 44.4,
          "en": "so the color and the font size,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.4,
          "end": 47.14,
          "en": "but the text itself should be dynamic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.14,
          "end": 49.44,
          "en": "Put in other words, it would be better",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 49.44,
          "end": 53.58,
          "en": "if in gradient container where we use style text,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 53.58,
          "end": 56.46,
          "en": "we could pass the text to style text",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 56.46,
          "end": 59.22,
          "en": "so that this can still be set in the place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 59.22,
          "end": 61.83,
          "en": "where we want to use our custom widget",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 61.83,
          "end": 65.67,
          "en": "instead of having it locked into our custom widget.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 65.67,
          "end": 68.28,
          "en": "And that's of course, a super common use case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 68.28,
          "end": 72,
          "en": "because most of your widgets should be reusable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 72,
          "end": 73.65,
          "en": "and should be flexible,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 73.65,
          "end": 76.74,
          "en": "and should be able to receive data from outside,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 76.74,
          "end": 79.98,
          "en": "like here where we pass data into styled text",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 79.98,
          "end": 82.203,
          "en": "from inside the gradient container widget.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 83.1,
          "end": 87.3,
          "en": "So how can we make our own custom widget reusable then?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 87.3,
          "end": 90.12,
          "en": "Well with help of the constructor function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 90.12,
          "end": 94.68,
          "en": "Because I mentioned before that here, when you use a class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 94.68,
          "end": 98.46000000000001,
          "en": "your own one or one provided by Flutter, doesn't matter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 98.46000000000001,
          "end": 102.09,
          "en": "with parentheses like this, which is how you have to use it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 102.09,
          "end": 104.34,
          "en": "in order to turn it into an object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 104.34,
          "end": 107.94,
          "en": "you're calling the constructor function of that class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 107.94,
          "end": 111.09,
          "en": "You get one automatically if your class doesn't have one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 111.09,
          "end": 114.45,
          "en": "Otherwise your own constructor function is called.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 114.45,
          "end": 116.82,
          "en": "Well, and since this is just a constructor function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 116.82,
          "end": 117.84,
          "en": "being called here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 117.84,
          "end": 120.72,
          "en": "if we want to be able to pass input values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 120.72,
          "end": 124.68,
          "en": "to that constructive function, we have to accept them here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 124.68,
          "end": 128.91,
          "en": "We are actually already accepting this named key argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 128.91,
          "end": 132.72,
          "en": "because we had to, to forward it to StatelessWidget,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 132.72,
          "end": 135.6,
          "en": "but we can accept more than just that key,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 135.6,
          "end": 139.5,
          "en": "either more named arguments by adding commas here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 139.5,
          "end": 142.29,
          "en": "and adding all the named arguments that we want to accept",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 142.29,
          "end": 144.63,
          "en": "between these curly braces,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 144.63,
          "end": 147.24,
          "en": "or in addition to these named arguments,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 147.24,
          "end": 151.95,
          "en": "also positional arguments before those curly braces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 151.95,
          "end": 155.43,
          "en": "So for example here, we could accept the text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 155.43,
          "end": 158.4,
          "en": "We then should also add a type annotation here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 158.4,
          "end": 161.88,
          "en": "to make it clear which type of value this should be.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 161.88,
          "end": 163.44,
          "en": "Otherwise it's dynamic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 163.44,
          "end": 166.5,
          "en": "and we typically wanna avoid that, as you learned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 166.5,
          "end": 169.623,
          "en": "And here it would be some string, which we want some text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 170.79,
          "end": 171.78,
          "en": "And with that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 171.78,
          "end": 176.04,
          "en": "we now are able to pass some text to style text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 176.04,
          "end": 176.94299999999998,
          "en": "This works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 178.68,
          "end": 182.7,
          "en": "However, with that, we are not using this text in here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 182.7,
          "end": 184.8,
          "en": "We are accepting the text here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 184.8,
          "end": 187.62,
          "en": "we're passing some text to style text,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 187.62,
          "end": 189.24,
          "en": "but this text argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 189.24,
          "end": 192.21,
          "en": "which we are accepting in our constructor function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 192.21,
          "end": 193.89,
          "en": "is now not being used here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 193.89,
          "end": 194.723,
          "en": "Instead,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 194.723,
          "end": 196.953,
          "en": "we still have the hard code 'Hello World!' down there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 197.91,
          "end": 200.4,
          "en": "So how can we use this argument?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 200.4,
          "end": 202.71,
          "en": "Well not by using its name here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 202.71,
          "end": 206.1,
          "en": "If we try to do that and we use the name text down here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 206.1,
          "end": 207.69,
          "en": "we get an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 207.69,
          "end": 209.94,
          "en": "We get an error because this argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 209.94,
          "end": 212.13,
          "en": "which we accept in the constructor function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 212.13,
          "end": 214.38,
          "en": "is not magically available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 214.38,
          "end": 216.48,
          "en": "in some other method of the class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 216.48,
          "end": 220.05,
          "en": "These two things are detached from each other",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 220.05,
          "end": 221.97,
          "en": "even though they're in the same class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 221.97,
          "end": 224.25,
          "en": "This is just how that works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 224.25,
          "end": 225.96,
          "en": "Instead, what we have to do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 225.96,
          "end": 229.38,
          "en": "is we have to add a so-called class variable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 229.38,
          "end": 232.62,
          "en": "a so-called property to this class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 232.62,
          "end": 236.52,
          "en": "So a variable, just like the variables we added before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 236.52,
          "end": 239.67000000000002,
          "en": "but now not outside of a class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 239.67000000000002,
          "end": 243.57,
          "en": "but instead inside of the class to which they should belong.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 243.57,
          "end": 247.593,
          "en": "So here for example, a variable, called output text,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 248.61,
          "end": 252.48,
          "en": "or just text, it can be the same name as this argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 252.48,
          "end": 253.533,
          "en": "That's no problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 254.4,
          "end": 258.48,
          "en": "So we can add this, and if we don't set it to a value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 258.48,
          "end": 261.36,
          "en": "as you learned, you should instead define",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 261.36,
          "end": 265.74,
          "en": "the value type here instead of using var.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 265.74,
          "end": 269.1,
          "en": "So here I'm just writing string text,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 269.1,
          "end": 272.13,
          "en": "and with that, we added a variable to this class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 272.13,
          "end": 276.9,
          "en": "and this variable is now available in all the methods.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 276.9,
          "end": 279,
          "en": "Of course, I'm still getting an error down here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 279,
          "end": 280.17,
          "en": "but here the error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 280.17,
          "end": 282.93,
          "en": "is now actually a different one than before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 282.93,
          "end": 285.21,
          "en": "If I remove this text variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 285.21,
          "end": 286.89,
          "en": "and we take a look at this error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 286.89,
          "end": 291.18,
          "en": "we see that now it doesn't even find anything called text,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 291.18,
          "end": 292.98,
          "en": "which makes sense, because as mentioned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 292.98,
          "end": 294.63,
          "en": "there is nothing named text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 294.63,
          "end": 296.4,
          "en": "This argument here doesn't count",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 296.4,
          "end": 297.84000000000003,
          "en": "because the constructor function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 297.84000000000003,
          "end": 299.64300000000003,
          "en": "and this method is not connected.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 300.6,
          "end": 304.08,
          "en": "If I add this variable here, I get a different error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 304.08,
          "end": 306.69,
          "en": "It's no longer saying that text is not known.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 306.69,
          "end": 310.47,
          "en": "Instead it's, well complaining about some other things here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 310.47,
          "end": 313.02,
          "en": "The reason for that is that now we do have this variable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 313.02,
          "end": 316.05,
          "en": "but in the end, this variable is still not set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 316.05,
          "end": 319.44,
          "en": "to the value we receive as a argument here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 319.44,
          "end": 321.63,
          "en": "To do this, we got two main ways.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 321.63,
          "end": 325.53,
          "en": "We can again add this colon here after our argument list,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 325.53,
          "end": 328.29,
          "en": "and then here we could refer to this text variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 328.29,
          "end": 331.05,
          "en": "by its name and set it equal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 331.05,
          "end": 333.72,
          "en": "to this text argument we're getting here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 333.72,
          "end": 336.12,
          "en": "So text equals text might look a bit strange,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 336.12,
          "end": 339.93,
          "en": "but the first text here refers to the text variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 339.93,
          "end": 343.47,
          "en": "The second text here refers to the text argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 343.47,
          "end": 345.75,
          "en": "So if I use different names here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 345.75,
          "end": 350.15999999999997,
          "en": "like output text here and here, this becomes clearer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 350.15999999999997,
          "end": 352.71,
          "en": "and I would also have to use it down here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 352.71,
          "end": 354.65,
          "en": "So now we would be setting our text",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 354.65,
          "end": 356.55,
          "en": "to this argument which we receive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 356.55,
          "end": 358.98,
          "en": "However, as before with super,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 358.98,
          "end": 361.17,
          "en": "this is unnecessarily verbose,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 361.17,
          "end": 363.39,
          "en": "and therefore Dart gives us a shortcut",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 363.39,
          "end": 365.46,
          "en": "because this is a very common pattern",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 365.46,
          "end": 368.19,
          "en": "that you receive a value on an argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 368.19,
          "end": 370.32,
          "en": "and you wanna store that in a variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 370.32,
          "end": 372.3,
          "en": "that belongs to the class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 372.3,
          "end": 376.86,
          "en": "You can replace this string part here with this dot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 376.86,
          "end": 380.43,
          "en": "so that this says this.text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 380.43,
          "end": 382.14,
          "en": "Now you just must make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 382.14,
          "end": 385.35,
          "en": "that your variable is also called text,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
